# desktop.pkgs — the tier for 2 GB and up, and the default on a Pi 4/5.
#
# XFCE because it is the heaviest desktop that is still honest about being
# light, and because its settings UI means the machine can be configured
# without a text editor.
xorg-minimal
xorg-fonts
# ⛔ glxinfo IS ITS OWN PACKAGE ON VOID — it is NOT part of mesa-demos, which
# this file used to claim. `xbps-install mesa-demos` then answers "already
# installed" while glxinfo is still missing, which reads as a broken install
# rather than a wrong package name. That claim cost a round trip on the
# Pentium 4 a second time, having been written to prevent the first.
#
# On hardware this old it is the first thing anyone needs: "is this the real
# driver or llvmpipe" is the question behind most performance complaints.
glxinfo
mesa-demos
# ⚠ Diagnosing a display problem on a machine you can only reach over ssh
# needs a way to see what is actually on screen. `xwd -id <win>` reads a
# window's contents even when the screen is DPMS-blanked, and wmctrl lists
# what exists — together they are how a game that "freezes" turns out to be a
# modal dialog nobody could see. Both are tiny.
xwd
wmctrl
xf86-input-libinput
xinit
xfce4
# ⚠ CAPITAL T, and the plugins are lowercase `thunar-*`. Lowercase `thunar` is
# not a package at all — and querying for it is how this file briefly claimed
# that xfce4 ships no file manager. It does: xfce4 depends on Thunar>=4.20 and
# thunar-volman. Both are named here anyway, because a metapackage's contents
# are not a promise, but neither was missing.
Thunar
thunar-volman
thunar-archive-plugin
# ⛔ THE REAL GAP: xfce4 pulls NEITHER gvfs NOR udisks2. Clicking a disk in a
# file manager goes through gvfs to udisks2, so without them an internal
# Windows partition simply never appears in the sidebar — the file manager is
# working perfectly and has nothing to show. The only route to the data was a
# manual mount as root.
gvfs
udisks2
xfce4-terminal
xfce4-pulseaudio-plugin
lightdm
lightdm-gtk3-greeter
pipewire
wireplumber
alsa-pipewire
NetworkManager
network-manager-applet
# ⚠ Without this a headless machine announces nothing and cannot be reached by
# name — `ember.local` does not resolve, and finding it means reading an IP off
# a TTY. nss-mdns is the half people forget: avahi alone advertises, but does
# not let this machine RESOLVE other .local names.
avahi
nss-mdns
# ⚠ ESR, NOT MAINLINE. On a Pentium 4 the browser is the heaviest thing the
# machine will ever run and the bottleneck is the CPU, not the RAM — so the
# release train that changes least often is worth more here than the newest
# engine. Mainline `firefox` is in the repository if it is ever wanted.
firefox-esr
mousepad
ristretto
